<!--
  Phase 2.1 — Tool Asset Seed
  ============================
  30 realistic shop-floor tool assets seeded as anchors for the
  Manufacturing Intelligence cron (`_cron_maintenance_sweep`, daily),
  the readiness check, and the tool-lifecycle board view.

  Organized in 5 groups:
    1. Panel Saw Blades   (6) — 3 in-service + 3 standby
    2. CNC Router Bits    (8) — compression / straight / spiral / V-groove
    3. Boring Bits        (6) — confirmat M6 + M8, hinge cup, drawer runner
    4. Edge-Bander Hot-Melt Heads (4) — 3 in-service + 1 spare
    5. Sanding Belts      (6) — 80 / 120 / 180 grit pairs

  Field/value notes (verified against
  southbrook_mrp_kitchen_tools/models/tool_asset.py):
    * `lifecycle_state` selection: new / available / in_use /
      needs_sharpening / needs_calibration / under_maintenance / etc.
      Brief's "in_service" maps → "available"; "standby" → "new".
    * `condition` selection: excellent / good / worn / dull / damaged /
      unsafe. Brief's "fair" → "worn"; "new" → "excellent".
    * `tool_category_id` is a *related, readonly* field driven by the
      tool product's category. So we seed a minimal master product per
      group and the category flows through.
    * `sharpening_interval_days`, `calibration_interval_days`,
      `estimated_unit_cost`, `replacement_cost` do NOT exist on the
      v19 model — silently skipped per brief guidance ("skip rather
      than crash the install").
    * `code` is sequence-defaulted to "New"; left unset here.
    * `noupdate="1"` so operators' manual edits to lifecycle / dates
      survive subsequent `-u` runs.
-->
<odoo>
    <data noupdate="1">

